# Production build config. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE — see below.
#
# Vite bakes VITE_* vars into the browser bundle at `vite build` time, so this
# cannot live in wrangler.jsonc `vars` (those are Worker RUNTIME vars and never
# reach the bundle). It has to be an env file, and `vite build` loads
# .env.production automatically in production mode.
#
# WHY IT IS SAFE TO COMMIT: the value is a same-origin path, not a credential.
# The wizard POSTs to /submit, the Worker (src/worker.ts) picks it up, attaches
# X-Home-Proxy-Secret from a Wrangler secret, and forwards to recruiting. The
# real credential is `wrangler secret put RECRUITING_INTAKE_SECRET` and is never
# in git or in the bundle.
#
# WHY IT IS COMMITTED AT ALL: this value used to be supplied only from an
# uncommitted local .env at deploy time, which meant the production build was
# not reproducible from the repo — a redeploy by anyone other than the last
# deployer silently broke submit, because api.ts throws when this is unset.
#
# DO NOT put the old Power Automate URL back here. It carries its trigger
# signature inline, so it is a capability URL — committing it would publish a
# credential. It is superseded by the Worker relay regardless.
VITE_JOB_ORDER_SUBMIT_URL=/submit
